Sleepers to transcend distance (culminating in the Internet) leads to a more homogeneous overall Consensus, as the influence of any given Sleeper can be spread far and wide. Ironically, the fact that the Consensus <i>isn't</i> homogeneous means that it's possible for localized reality zones to suffer from various types of Quiet: the entry for Irrationality Zones (under <i>Localized Reality</i>) ends with a mention of Irrationality Zones that have succumbed to Denial; and more generally, Irrationality Zones can be thought of as pockets of the Consensus that have succumbed to Quiet, usually manifesting as Madness. <br /> <br /> But third, you have Earthly Foundations: aspects of reality that prove stubbornly resistant to the influence of the Consensus. There are several schools of thought about why Earthly Foundations exist: there may indeed be certain truths that are hardwired into reality, and are innately true (what MRev referred to as Cosmological Constants; the opening paragraphs of Technocratic Reality implies that much of modern physics is in fact this kind of Earthly Foundation, with technomagick being an extrapolation on innate truths built into the fabric of reality); there may be influences from other times that are strong enough to endure even in the face of an opposing Consensus today (Historical Inertia; note that the nature of Time is such that the past influences the future much more readily than vice versa); and there may be inhuman entities capable of influencing reality, such as the Greater Spirit Entities mentioned on pp.486\u2013487 or rare Lesser Entities (same pages) that have somehow acquired Avatar-like abilities (arguably, the Technocray's efforts to strengthen the Gauntlet are as much to isolate Conventional Space from these ultraterrestrial influences, granting the Consensus of humanity more of a monopoly on this side of the barrier \u2014 which is only effective to the extent that the entity in question is confined to the other side). But regardless of <i>why</i>, the result is the same: there are some things that will be true (or false, as the case may be) even if the local consensus of humanity says otherwise. Note that this allows for a more widespread version of the aforementioned \u201cpockets of Quiet\u201d: an overall disbelief in an Earthly Foundation is arguably an overall case of Consensual Denial. <br /> <br /> That third point is especially significant, since it drives home an important truth \u2014 that the Consensus and Reality are <i>not</i> interchangeable terms: the Consensus <i>influences</i> Reality, just as the Awakened do; but it doesn't <i>define</i> Reality. Put more bluntly, Reality doesn't need Magick. This is something that mages generally don't dwell on, since accepting it requires a humility that tends to run counter to the pride that exists at the heart of Magick. But just because you don't believe something, that doesn't make it false.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good analysis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T05:59:55-08:00","id":799561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/798518-the-nature-of-the-consensus#post798518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the nature of the Consensus?<br /> <br /> But third, you have Earthly Foundations: aspects of reality that prove stubbornly resistant to the influence of the Consensus. There are several schools of thought about why Earthly Foundations exist: there may indeed be certain truths that are hardwired into reality, and are innately true (what MRev referred to as Cosmological Constants; the opening paragraphs of Technocratic Reality implies that much of modern physics is in fact this kind of Earthly Foundation, with technomagick being an extrapolation on innate truths built into the fabric of reality); there may be influences from other times that are strong enough to endure even in the face of an opposing Consensus today (Historical Inertia; note that the nature of Time is such that the past influences the future much more readily than vice versa); and there may be inhuman entities capable of influencing reality, such as the Greater Spirit Entities mentioned on pp.486\u2013487 or rare Lesser Entities (same pages) that have somehow acquired Avatar-like abilities (arguably, the Technocray's efforts to strengthen the Gauntlet are as much to isolate Conventional Space from these ultraterrestrial influences, granting the Consensus of humanity more of a monopoly on this side of the barrier \u2014 which is only effective to the extent that the entity in question is confined to the other side). But regardless of <i>why</i>, the result is the same: there are some things that will be true (or false, as the case may be) even if the local consensus of humanity says otherwise. Note that this allows for a more widespread version of the aforementioned \u201cpockets of Quiet\u201d: an overall disbelief in an Earthly Foundation is arguably an overall case of Consensual Denial.</div> </div> </div> </div>An interesting point a friend had made is that some books seemed to hint that the earthly foundations are maintained by the Celestine level spirits and above, and given the list of &quot;Awakened&quot; spirits from previous editions it seemed entirely possible. <br /> <br /> Though that would mean a mage technically Can move the moon, he just has to ask luna's permission first, a scary concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T06:59:52-08:00","id":799580,"title":"","content":"That's somethig I was thinking for a while. If there were no humans, there would be no consensus, but there would still exist a reality. A default one. Consensus don't create reality only slightly shape it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T08:03:21-08:00","id":799614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/798518-the-nature-of-the-consensus?p=799561#post799561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An interesting point a friend had made is that some books seemed to hint that the earthly foundations are maintained by the Celestine level spirits and above, and given the list of \u201cAwakened\u201d spirits from previous editions it seemed entirely possible. <br /> <br /> Though that would mean a mage technically Can move the moon, he just has to ask luna's permission first, a scary concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>The distinction between Earthly Foundations that simply are and Earthly Foundations that are the result of a Greater Spirit Entity is very fuzzy, and in practical terms not all that important. But it's the sort of thing that a Chorister and a Void Engineer might argue about, with the Chorister arguing that all Earthly Foundations are ultimately there by the Will of the One and the Void Engineer arguing that they're all innate properties of the Void. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/798518-the-nature-of-the-consensus?p=799580#post799580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's somethig I was thinking for a while. If there were no humans, there would be no consensus, but there would still exist a reality. A default one. Consensus don't create reality only slightly shape it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right; though I wouldn't put the word \u201cslightly\u201d in there: the changes that the Consensus imposes on Reality can be extensive and enduring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T10:05:07-08:00","id":799680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/798518-the-nature-of-the-consensus?p=799580#post799580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's somethig I was thinking for a while. If there were no humans, there would be no consensus, but there would still exist a reality. A default one. Consensus don't create reality only slightly shape it.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/798518-the-nature-of-the-consensus?p=799614#post799614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right; though I wouldn't put the word \u201cslightly\u201d in there: the changes that the Consensus imposes on Reality can be extensive and enduring.</div> </div> </div> </div>The consensus is powerful enough that, according to some, it turned an area once filled with Ether, traversable by mere airships and holding several inhabited, mysterious worlds into a dark, cold vacuum and dead rocks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 01-03-2016, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T13:19:06-08:00","id":799771,"title":"","content":"Personally I like to think of Consensus as a point of view and that it is the subjective point of view of reality by the masses. What makes Mages special is that they are able to alter their point of view giving them a better or just different look at reality. Think of a cylinder, from one side it looks like a rectangle(masses and Consensus) but from another it looks like a circle(a Mage).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T13:19:45-08:00","id":799772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/798518-the-nature-of-the-consensus?p=799680#post799680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The consensus is powerful enough that, according to some, it turned an area once filled with Ether, traversable by mere airships and holding several inhabited, mysterious worlds into a dark, cold vacuum and dead rocks.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a rote for that (in the Void Engineer Convention Book).<br /> <br /> These days, the event you're talking about is the ongoing spread of Conventional Space, which has moved from the edge of the atmosphere to the orbit of the moon to the asteroid belt. Etherspace still exists; its just not as accessible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-03-2016, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T16:04:10-08:00","id":799845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/798518-the-nature-of-the-consensus?p=799680#post799680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The consensus is powerful enough that, according to some, it turned an area once filled with Ether, traversable by mere airships and holding several inhabited, mysterious worlds into a dark, cold vacuum and dead rocks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did it, though? One could argue that it just shunted people into the Umbra by default before and now shunts them into the real space.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T20:30:18-08:00","id":800936,"title":"","content":"Even if that's the case, it managed to make a relatively niche almost unvisited layer of the Umbra part of the Gaia Realm and locked all other layers behind the Gauntlet.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> How I interpret the Consensus amounts to it being a Spirit 4/DSci 4-like effect that, instead of being Vulgar and just outright overriding local 'amplitudes' of possible models of reality, it 'nudges' them in favor of the source human's beliefs. However, because humans can and do relate to one another, and form societies with rules, these inclinations tend to reinforce in response to one another - at least, in rejection of something that &quot;breaks the rules&quot;. An individual's influence is generally 'washed out' by the giant tumult of either neutralizing or reinforcing beliefs in the general area, and isn't usually strong enough on its own when there isn't a Consensus. This also affects things like vampires and Bygones, to a degree. (Werewolves, of course, are so heavily rooted via the Delirium that they're nearly immune.)<br /> <br /> The Earthly Foundations are <i>generally</i> not affected by this - they've been part of human experience for so long that we almost instinctively accept them and support them.<br /> <br /> By this model, a Quiet Consensus is effectively a Consensus web that actively rejects other Consensus webs, and possibly the Earthly Foundations. The latter would be baaaaad, in much the way a Quiet 10 Marauder is - they're effectively pushing themselves away from the Earth's shared basis of understanding.<br /> <br /> The Gauntlet is the wall between the possibilities that are acceptable, and the possibilities that are rejected but still 'there', though it's also a different 'location'. The Umbra is weird like that.<br /> <br /> All Mages still generate Consensus to a degree - after all, the Umbra looks how you expect it to a large part of the time - though most are sufficiently open to &quot;weird shit going on&quot; that it's no more noticeable than any individual Sleeper's influence on the Consensus, and doesn't cause Paradox to backlash. The exceptions to the 'open to weird shit' are Sleepwalkers - who are basically just like normal Sleepers except where 'accepted' things are concerned - and Marauders, who are surrounded in a constant &quot;forceful&quot; Consensus effect of own delusions.<br /> <br /> In absence of the Consensus's greater support net, reality defaults back to either Earthly/Solar Foundations (in the case of the Gaiasphere and Near Umbra) or true Cosmological Constants. That's partly the explanation for 'variations' in the Curse of Caine - the core can't be changed, but added disadvantages or a bit of easing the original curse for conforming to the myths might be possible. A human in the Umbra will alter it only insofar as their perceptions - they don't have enough 'grip' to actually force the surroundings instead of being pushed toward a perceptual layer. Unless they're a Marauder.<br /> <br /> Fucking Marauders.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> It's also worth note that Consensus paradigm shifts don't just establish tremendous effects and shift how normal reality behaves, they also can change how magick itself behaves to a degree. Blowing up a castle wall might have used to be a Forces 5 effect, where nowadays it's Forces 3 or (with a mundane piece of artillery that isn't quite up to the task) 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6072,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","user":"Quantumboost","date":". 01-07-2016, 02:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T22:06:18-08:00","id":801022,"title":"","content":"On that note, M20 kind of actually finally gives somewhat of a RAW number of people that a Mage requires to go 'I do believe', in order to turn a vulgar effect into a very localized coincidence for a ritual.<br /> <br /> Page 342:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you\u2019ve got over 100 people involved, certain vulgar<br /> Effects (summonings, gateways, raisings of the dead,<br /> and so forth) may be considered coincidental if there<br /> are no other witnesses around to contradict that impression.<br /> A solitary rite on the Moors is far more effective in that<br /> regard than a concert in a nightclub downtown. </div> </div> </div>This of course is not the same as areas where a small culture or tribe has established their own consensus over time, or that simply has been untouched by modern society in a while..those are something different; This is sudden and temporary, a way to subvert the consensus of an area for a single act with a very large cult...hence a single witness being able to disrupt it all as the normal local state of consensus just needs one of its mental associates to witness and go '<i>wat'</i> in order to ruin the effort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T15:15:04-07:00","id":1491351,"title":"","content":"Heading some links from another thread that where I discuss the subject more in depth. I will be revising this post soon, when I have more time for more details.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1479349-st-theories-why-did-magic-start-to-fail-in-da-mage?p=1479352#post1479352\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...52#post1479352</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1479349-st-theories-why-did-magic-start-to-fail-in-da-mage?p=1479379#post1479379\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...79#post1479379</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1479349-st-theories-why-did-magic-start-to-fail-in-da-mage?p=1479443#post1479443\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...43#post1479443</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1479349-st-theories-why-did-magic-start-to-fail-in-da-mage?p=1479459#post1479459\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...59#post1479459</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1479349-st-theories-why-did-magic-start-to-fail-in-da-mage?p=1479550#post1479550\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...50#post1479550</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1479349-st-theories-why-did-magic-start-to-fail-in-da-mage?p=1479552#post1479552\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...52#post1479552</a><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1479349-st-theories-why-did-magic-start-to-fail-in-da-mage?p=1479702#post1479702\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1479349-st-theories-why-did-magic-start-to-fail-in-da-mage?p=1479702#post1479702\"> ST Theories: Why did magic start to fail in DA Mage? - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1479349-st-theories-why-did-magic-start-to-fail-in-da-mage?p=1479702#post1479702\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1479349-st-theories-why-did-magic-start-to-fail-in-da-mage?p=1479702#post1479702 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> One of the things that I found while browsing the internet was that a large portion of the world Still believes in magic in some form. At least 30% of americans believe in astrology, 41% believe n psychic powers, 42% believe in some form os new-age spiritual energy(not counting astrology or psychic powers), 85% of the human race is religious, Ireland Still doesn't pave over fairy circles because old beliefs are held by the majority even in public office, etc. And that is all just Modern Belief in the IRL version of earth, which is suppose to be orders of magnitude less superstitious and well adjusted </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-25-2022, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T07:56:18-07:00","id":1491420,"title":"","content":"I'm usually not into necro, but this is a useful topic. A lot of people seem to believe that existence is all wibbly wobbly in Mage, and it's ovbviously not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T07:42:45-07:00","id":1491474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/798518-the-nature-of-the-consensus?p=1491420#post1491420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm usually not into necro, but this is a useful topic. A lot of people seem to believe that existence is all wibbly wobbly in Mage, and it's ovbviously not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which just makes the game become even more of a mess than it is. So, where is the line drawned in the sand? Is gravity real real, but what about electromagnetism? What about strong and weak nuclear forces?<br /> <br /> Is Relativity real? Because, you know, it makes no sense for gravity to be real but not Relativity. Unless gravity is some sort of super Spirit that enjoys pulling everything to the Earth's center because of reasons.<br /> <br /> This approach of saying that things are half matter, half &quot;imagination&quot; just simply do NOT work, and it would be preferable if everything was a code on the Matrix or Vishnu's dream.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T08:01:39-07:00","id":1491476,"title":"","content":"The distinction in terms of relevancy in the setting is between \u201cwhat things are true because that's what the Consensus says?\u201d and \u201cwhat things are true <i>independent of</i> what the Consensus says?\u201d I make no judgment on <i>why</i> the latter is a thing; only that it <i>is</i> a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T08:16:52-07:00","id":1491479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/798518-the-nature-of-the-consensus?p=1491474#post1491474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which just makes the game become even more of a mess than it is. So, where is the line drawn in the sand? Is gravity real, but what about electromagnetism? What about strong and weak nuclear forces?<br /> <br /> Is Relativity real? Because, you know, it makes no sense for gravity to be real but not Relativity. Unless gravity is some sort of super Spirit that enjoys pulling everything to the Earth's center because of reasons.<br /> <br /> This approach of saying that things are half matter, half &quot;imagination&quot; just simply do NOT work, and it would be preferable if everything was a code on the Matrix or Vishnu's dream.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, the answer to these questions is whatever the storyteller and players decide. I think that the limits were left ambiguous, so each table can tailor the games to their liking. It's something that should be discussed beforehand to avoid confusion since, as you said, it can be quite a mess if you don't define the limits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T09:14:11-07:00","id":1491481,"title":"","content":"In terms of physics, Earthly Foundations generally operate on a \u201cbroad strokes\u201d principle. Things that the Earthly Foundations ensure to be Vulgar are, among other things, \u201cObvious violations of normal physical laws\u201d:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">water running uphill, people flying around, free floating molecules abruptly manifesting as solid mass, turtles suddenly moving at cheetah speed\u2026</div>One implication of this phrasing is that if the violation of physics <i>isn't</i> obvious, then it isn't proscribed by an Earthly Foundation. <br /> <br /> I don't think that there's a sharp delineation; rather, there's a continuum between effects dominated by Earthly Foundations and effects dominated by the Consensus. <br /> <br /> Also, keep in mind that this business of Earthly Foundations rarely affects Awakened workings beyond influencing where the line between Coincidental and Vulgar is drawn: that is, Earthly Foundations generally don't make things <i>impossible</i> for mages to do; they only make them <i>Paradoxical</i>. The only <i>limits</i> on what a mage can do comes from her <i>own</i> beliefs of what's possible with her Magick. Reality Zones can make things easier or harder, safer or riskier; but they can never outright <i>prohibit</i> an effect.<br /> <br /> On the other hand: for Sleepers, that line between Coincidental and Vulgar <i>is</i> the line between possible and impossible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-27-2022, 12:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T10:36:16-07:00","id":1491495,"title":"","content":"Well, phenomenomoligical reality doesnt require Magick any more than it requires sapient beings, but Mage seems to imply that all of reality, the Prime, is alive and has it's own will. I forget what book it's in but there's an example of an Akashic who discusses a fist smashing a stone, and how both are an inherent unity. Everything is cosmic mind and therefore everything is aware.<br /> <br /> Choristers, Akashics and Khavadi would laugh at this whole &quot;reality&quot; vs &quot;consensus&quot; stuff, and say that there is no difference between actor and acted upon. All action is magick, even things like when a star collapses into a black hole or other functions of physics. Talk about &quot;consensus&quot; is simply what <i>humans</i> think reality is, and there's lots more reality than there are humans. The air, rocks and space have opinions too. The reason why the anthropocentric view of the Union is so limited is because it centers only a very small section of the universe in it - human beings.<br /> <br /> This also neatly explains why there will always be Scourge/Paradox - just because you desire and believe that thinks are a certain way, the rest of the cosmos may not. The Consensus is just the rest of humanity helping or hindering you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","user":"Robert Armsley","date":". 08-27-2022, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T10:55:16-07:00","id":1491496,"title":"","content":"Yep. And that's <i>one</i> perfectly valid interpretation: say that the Earthly Foundations are simply the result of nonhuman willworkers, which have enough influence to keep the mass of humanity from dominating. <br /> <br /> But it's not <i>the</i> answer. Setting it as \u201cthe\u201d answer makes the Choristers, Akashics, and Kha'vadi objectively right, and those who disagree with them objectively wrong. <br /> <br /> That's why I strive to maintain an \u201cagnostic\u201d attitude toward the issue: the Earthly Foundations exist; that much is fact. But <i>the reason they exist</i> is one of those things that's open to interpretation, and which different factions can disagree about without one side being right and the others being wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T11:34:03-07:00","id":1491502,"title":"","content":"The Earthly Foundations don't even say something is impossible for normal humans. They just say something <i>must have a reason</i> to not work as intended.<br /> <br /> Simplest example (not the only one): anything that flies. Gravity, or at least <i>falling</i>, is an Earthly Foundation. Under no circumstance it simply <i>ceases to exist</i>. Instead, it is the default state until something defies it within reason. Like birds, balloons and planes do all the time.<br /> <br /> What is able to defy an Earthly Foundation may very well be shaped by Consensus, the important factor is that the Foundation can't be simply ignored, it must be worked around. And Magic can be this workaround, although if it doesn't <i>seems</i> to be good enough, it will incur Paradox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":". 08-27-2022, 07:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T16:11:26-07:00","id":1491524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/798518-the-nature-of-the-consensus?p=1491496#post1491496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep. And that's <i>one</i> perfectly valid interpretation: say that the Earthly Foundations are simply the result of nonhuman willworkers, which have enough influence to keep the mass of humanity from dominating.<br /> <br /> But it's not <i>the</i> answer. Setting it as \u201cthe\u201d answer makes the Choristers, Akashics, and Kha'vadi objectively right, and those who disagree with them objectively wrong.<br /> <br /> That's why I strive to maintain an \u201cagnostic\u201d attitude toward the issue: the Earthly Foundations exist; that much is fact. But <i>the reason they exist</i> is one of those things that's open to interpretation, and which different factions can disagree about without one side being right and the others being wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the best way to do it, I think. Like the Antediluvians in Vampire, the mysteries of the Tapestry and the Tellurian should always subject to question. Truth Until Paradox!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T17:04:52-07:00","id":1491533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/798518-the-nature-of-the-consensus?p=1491502#post1491502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Earthly Foundations don't even say something is impossible for normal humans. They just say something <i>must have a reason</i> to not work as intended.<br /> <br /> Simplest example (not the only one): anything that flies. Gravity, or at least <i>falling</i>, is an Earthly Foundation. Under no circumstance it simply <i>ceases to exist</i>. Instead, it is the default state until something defies it within reason. Like birds, balloons and planes do all the time.<br /> <br /> What is able to defy an Earthly Foundation may very well be shaped by Consensus, the important factor is that the Foundation can't be simply ignored, it must be worked around. And Magic can be this workaround, although if it doesn't <i>seems</i> to be good enough, it will incur Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>This actually has some implications worth considering. What you're really talking about is using some accepted elements of a Reality Zone to counter principles of the Earthly Foundations, such as using \u201chot air rises\u201d to counter \u201cthings fall down\u201d (result: hot air balloons). This could be called \u201cscience\u201d (in lower case, to distinguish it from the Enlightened Science of the Technocracy or the Awakened Science of the Etherites). I'm still thinking through the implications of this; especially in terms of how or if Sorcery factors into it. But even without Sorcery, this balancing act between Earthly Foundations and Coincidental Reality doesn't necessarily have to be science as we would describe it today: the hot air balloon example could also be justified in the four elements model of reality, where Earth-like things fall and Fire-like things rise.<br /> <br /> Anyway, just some rough thoughts for now. Gotta get back to work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-31-2023, 11:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T17:45:26-07:00","id":1491538,"title":"","content":"Sorcery and the Consensus: <br /> <br /> Sorcery isn't Awakened Magick. It is its own thing, despite a handful of suggested links between them (e.g., an optional section in S20 and S:PoP that allows mages to create Sorcery Paths, and speculation in the original edition of Sorcerer that Hedge Magic is associated with mythic threads). That means how, or even <i>if</i>, Sorcery relates to the Consensus need not have anything to do with how Awakened Magick relates to the Consensus. That said, there <i>are</i> parallels: though the terms aren't used, the rules for Sorcery acknowledge a Coincidental/Vulgar divide, just like Awakened Magick does. But instead of generating Paradox, the effect of Path Magic being \u201cobvious\u201d manifests entirely on the form of the casting being more likely to fail in the presents witnesses: S20 has a chart suggesting how many successes to cancel out based on how public the obvious working is. If the working is subtle enough, though, it can be performed in times square with no hindrance.<br /> <br /> What this means is that the relationship between sorcery and the consensus is more complicated than just saying that sorcery is effectively Coincidental. It may not be awakened magic, but sorcery still allows you to do things that the reality zone would prohibit to the fully mundane.<br /> <br /> In terms of my previous post, what this means is that sorcery doesn't factor into the issue of using coincidental reality to offset and Earthly Foundation, any more than awakened magic does: both will allow you to override the Earthly Foundation; but doing so with either of them is, in one sense or another, vulgar. Or, if it's Coincidental, is only because the Reality Zone has already made it Coincidental.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-27-2022, 08:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T18:21:21-07:00","id":1491542,"title":"","content":"Getting back to the consensus itself, an important question that does not have an official answer as far as I know is how or even if the earthly foundations can be changed. All that's known is that it's a lot harder to do that than it is to change the Consensus.<br /> <br /> And we do have a mechanism available for changing the consensus. It comes in two parts: the \u201cShifting the Zone\u201d section in M20, and the optional Terranorming system in the Operative's Dossier. The former is the purely mundane actions needed to bring about a paradigm shift in a community; and the latter has to do with how to translate that shift into an actual change in the Reality Zone. This process involves a technique called \u201cRepriming\u201d, which can be thought of as a way to \u201csoften\u201d the metaphysical space and make it more amenable to changes. After you complete your terranorming, you then \u201ccap the Zone\u201d, finalizing the changes and \u201chardening\u201d the Zone to make it as resistant to change as it used to be.<br /> <br /> Changing Earthly foundations, on the other hand, likely depends on the nature of Earthly Foundation \u2014 that topic that I have been trying to avoid up until now.<br /> <br /> \u2022 If the Earthly foundations are the results of some sort of greater spiritual entities such as the triad or a supreme being, then simply convincing people to change their minds will never be enough; the \u201cshifting The Zone\u201d part of the process will have to involve convincing said greater spiritual entities to change <i>their</i> minds \u2014 which, in practice, is probably equivalent to it being impossible.<br /> <br /> \u2022 If the Earthly foundations, on the other hand, are built into the \u201cweave\u201d of the Tapestry, then some means of \u201creweaving\u201d the Tapestry must be found. I would take inspiration from The Acts of imperium described in the Mage The Awakening supplement, imperial mysteries. Specifically, in order to make changes to the fundamental nature of reality, an archmaster must first change what amounts to the consensus to align with the changes that she wants to make; and then she needs to perform a massive working involving Archmagic in order to impress the change in the Consensus into the Earthly Foundations.<br /> <br /> \u2022 If the Earthly foundations are \u201cmerely\u201d exceptionally stubborn pieces of the Consensus, then altering the Earthly foundations may be as \u201csimple\u201d as using the Terra norming process at an increased difficulty.<br /> <br /> The second and third of these approaches could use very similar mechanics; the main difference would be that in the second case, the \u201cincreased difficulty\u201d would come from the \u201cRepriming\u201d needed to make Earthly Foundations malleable requiring Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022 (or more). I could see generalizing this to apply to all three of the views outlined above, although the first might better be served with some sort of Spirit \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022 or higher that lets you influence Greater Spiritual Entities. (Alternately, I could see the Void Engineers using Dimensional Science \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022 or higher to accomplish this while using what amounts to the second option.)<br /> <br /> Basically, the idea is that changes in the Consensus cannot translate to changes in the Earthly Foundations without the intervention of Archmagic; and changing the Earthly Foundations <i>without</i> first changing the Consensus should be difficult even for archmasters. (I'm operating on the basis that nothing is <i>truly</i> impossible for them; but some things will be harder than others.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-31-2023, 11:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T09:05:44-07:00","id":1491605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Armsley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/798518-the-nature-of-the-consensus?p=1491495#post1491495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, phenomenomoligical reality doesnt require Magick any more than it requires sapient beings, but Mage seems to imply that all of reality, the Prime, is alive and has it's own will. I forget what book it's in but there's an example of an Akashic who discusses a fist smashing a stone, and how both are an inherent unity. Everything is cosmic mind and therefore everything is aware.<br /> <br /> Choristers, Akashics and Khavadi would laugh at this whole &amp;quot;reality&amp;quot; vs &amp;quot;consensus&amp;quot; stuff, and say that there is no difference between actor and acted upon. All action is magick, even things like when a star collapses into a black hole or other functions of physics. Talk about &amp;quot;consensus&amp;quot; is simply what <i>humans</i> think reality is, and there's lots more reality than there are humans. The air, rocks and space have opinions too. The reason why the anthropocentric view of the Union is so limited is because it centers only a very small section of the universe in it - human beings.<br /> <br /> This also neatly explains why there will always be Scourge/Paradox - just because you desire and believe that thinks are a certain way, the rest of the cosmos may not. The Consensus is just the rest of humanity helping or hindering you.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has always been my interpretation too. That the universe of MtA works as a sort of living organism, and that humanity is just a part of the whole. The air has opinions too, and both air and water agrees that air should be lighter than water, and both have come to an agreement with earth that they must weight less than the last. Not so much that those are bound by molecules and atoms to behave in the way they do, but more that those are their &quot;spiritual contracts&quot; from the dawn of creation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/798518-the-nature-of-the-consensus?p=1491496#post1491496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep. And that's <i>one</i> perfectly valid interpretation: say that the Earthly Foundations are simply the result of nonhuman willworkers, which have enough influence to keep the mass of humanity from dominating. <br /> <br /> But it's not <i>the</i> answer. Setting it as \u201cthe\u201d answer makes the Choristers, Akashics, and Kha'vadi objectively right, and those who disagree with them objectively wrong. <br /> <br /> That's why I strive to maintain an \u201cagnostic\u201d attitude toward the issue: the Earthly Foundations exist; that much is fact. But <i>the reason they exist</i> is one of those things that's open to interpretation, and which different factions can disagree about without one side being right and the others being wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Im glad you posted this, because it perfectly adds to my previous response.<br /> <br /> Lets say for a moment that water and air are fluid because that's how the &quot;great spirits of water and air&quot; view themselves to be; let us call it the &quot;Spiritual Consensus&quot; for a moment.<br /> <br /> Now, I do have to ask this: can the &quot;Great Spirit of Water&quot; view itself as anything other than being fluid?<br /> <br /> Could the &quot;Spiritual Consensus&quot; be changed on it's own accord?<br /> <br /> Or, to better illustrate my point, could a lion decide to become a vegetarian?<br /> <br /> Those &quot;constants&quot; or &quot;Earthly Foundations&quot; are as mental as anything else, however they cannot be changed regardless of that fact; it's all &quot;Dreamscape&quot; (Im not making reference to The Dreaming or the Dream Zone/Maia, I mean it in a metaphysical sense, as in &quot;Vishnu's dream&quot;).<br /> <br /> However, those aspects of the mental landscape are essentiatly immutable; they are therefore, by the very definition of the word, <b>constants</b>.<br /> <br /> Does it make any practical difference thus if those Foundations are a sort of cosmological &quot;building blocks&quot; of Creation that therefore are immutable, or if they are the result of &quot;conscious&quot; effort by the part of the universal mind?<br /> <br /> Because in truth, they can be BOTH.<br /> <br /> And, both Chorists, Akashs and other and the Technos arw BOTH right at the same time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T12:20:51-07:00","id":1491632,"title":"","content":"<i>Or</i> both <i>wrong</i>. <br /> <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">It was six men of Indostan, to learning much inclined,<br /> who went to see the elephant (Though all of them were blind),<br /> that each by observation, might satisfy his mind.<br /> <br /> The first approached the elephant, and, happening to fall,<br /> against his broad and sturdy side, at once began to bawl:<br /> &quot;God bless me! but the elephant, is nothing but a wall!&quot;<br /> <br /> The second feeling of the tusk, cried: &quot;Ho! what have we here,<br /> so very round and smooth and sharp? To me tis mighty clear,<br /> this wonder of an elephant, is very like a spear!&quot;<br /> <br /> The third approached the animal, and, happening to take,<br /> the squirming trunk within his hands, &quot;I see,&quot; quoth he,<br /> the elephant is very like a snake!&quot;<br /> <br /> The fourth reached out his eager hand, and felt about the knee:<br /> &quot;What most this wondrous beast is like, is mighty plain,&quot; quoth he;<br /> &quot;Tis clear enough the elephant is very like a tree.&quot;<br /> <br /> The fifth, who chanced to touch the ear, Said; &quot;E'en the blindest man<br /> can tell what this resembles most; Deny the fact who can,<br /> This marvel of an elephant, is very like a fan!&quot;<br /> <br /> The sixth no sooner had begun, about the beast to grope,<br /> than, seizing on the swinging tail, that fell within his scope,<br /> &quot;I see,&quot; quothe he, &quot;the elephant is very like a rope!&quot;<br /> <br /> And so these men of Indostan, disputed loud and long,<br /> each in his own opinion, exceeding stiff and strong,<br /> Though each was partly in the right, and all were in the wrong!<br /> <br /> So, oft in theologic wars, the disputants, I ween,<br /> tread on in utter ignorance, of what each other mean,<br /> and prate about the elephant, not one of them has seen!<br /> <br /> John Godfrey Sax</div><br /> It's typical Awakened hubris to think that you know, or even <i>can</i> know, all the answers. And it's entirely possible that the final step of Ascension \u2014 and the reason why it's so hard to Ascend \u2014 is to fully embrace the truth of just how <i>little</i> you know. Kind of like a Chinese Finger Puzzle, it's only then that the former mage can truly open her eyes and see the world for what it <i>really</i> is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T12:38:46-07:00","id":1491636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/798518-the-nature-of-the-consensus?p=1491632#post1491632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Or</i> both <i>wrong</i>. <br /> <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">It was six men of Indostan, to learning much inclined,<br /> who went to see the elephant (Though all of them were blind),<br /> that each by observation, might satisfy his mind.<br /> <br /> The first approached the elephant, and, happening to fall,<br /> against his broad and sturdy side, at once began to bawl:<br /> &amp;quot;God bless me! but the elephant, is nothing but a wall!&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> The second feeling of the tusk, cried: &amp;quot;Ho! what have we here,<br /> so very round and smooth and sharp? To me tis mighty clear,<br /> this wonder of an elephant, is very like a spear!&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> The third approached the animal, and, happening to take,<br /> the squirming trunk within his hands, &amp;quot;I see,&amp;quot; quoth he,<br /> the elephant is very like a snake!&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> The fourth reached out his eager hand, and felt about the knee:<br /> &amp;quot;What most this wondrous beast is like, is mighty plain,&amp;quot; quoth he;<br /> &amp;quot;Tis clear enough the elephant is very like a tree.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> The fifth, who chanced to touch the ear, Said; &amp;quot;E'en the blindest man<br /> can tell what this resembles most; Deny the fact who can,<br /> This marvel of an elephant, is very like a fan!&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> The sixth no sooner had begun, about the beast to grope,<br /> than, seizing on the swinging tail, that fell within his scope,<br /> &amp;quot;I see,&amp;quot; quothe he, &amp;quot;the elephant is very like a rope!&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> And so these men of Indostan, disputed loud and long,<br /> each in his own opinion, exceeding stiff and strong,<br /> Though each was partly in the right, and all were in the wrong!<br /> <br /> So, oft in theologic wars, the disputants, I ween,<br /> tread on in utter ignorance, of what each other mean,<br /> and prate about the elephant, not one of them has seen!<br /> <br /> John Godfrey Sax</div><br /> It's typical Awakened hubris to think that you know, or even <i>can</i> know, all the answers. And it's entirely possible that the final step of Ascension \u2014 and the reason why it's so hard to Ascend \u2014 is to fully embrace the truth of just how <i>little</i> you know. Kind of like a Chinese Finger Puzzle, it's only then that the former mage can truly open her eyes and see the world for what it <i>really</i> is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beautifully said. Obviously, they cant all be right at the same time - at least, not entirely right at least.<br /> <br /> But they can indeed, be all wrong. Or at best, be all of them partially right and partially wrong too, seeing parts and mistaking those for the whole.<br /> <br /> I heard that story of the blind men and the elephant before as a child, but it were a translated version since I didnt know english at the time; so, I didnt know it's poetic composition, thank you for that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T12:23:55-07:00","id":1491938,"title":"","content":"Enjoying reading the thread. Honestly I've always felt like &quot;reality is 100% defined by consensus in mage! it's all wibbly wobbly! woah man, it's like, super malleable!&quot; isn't an opinion held in good faith by many. It sounds kind of cool, and it sounds deep, but it doesn't add up to a setting that makes any sense. You need to apply 100 levels of special pleading to make a world that looks even vaguely like the WoD, vaguely like our own, since so many basic facts of our world and the WoD don't match up to the idea that consensus directly alters all reality (even with 'Mage Prime').<br /> <br /> Essentially:<br /> <br /> Consensus shifting certain aspects of reality (Gauntlet, whether things are Vulgar, Mythic Threads, the High and sometimes Middle Umbra, Dreaming, social constructs like economies): has loads of evidence, makes sense, adds up to a setting that makes sense.<br /> <br /> Consensus controls everything and it's all wibbly wobbly: <i>Marge Simpson holding a potato</i> &quot;I just think it's neat!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T19:22:21-07:00","id":1491971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/798518-the-nature-of-the-consensus?p=1491938#post1491938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Enjoying reading the thread. Honestly I've always felt like &amp;quot;reality is 100% defined by consensus in mage! it's all wibbly wobbly! woah man, it's like, super malleable!&amp;quot; isn't an opinion held in good faith by many. It sounds kind of cool, and it sounds deep, but it doesn't add up to a setting that makes any sense. You need to apply 100 levels of special pleading to make a world that looks even vaguely like the WoD, vaguely like our own, since so many basic facts of our world and the WoD don't match up to the idea that consensus directly alters all reality (even with 'Mage Prime').<br /> <br /> Essentially:<br /> <br /> Consensus shifting certain aspects of reality (Gauntlet, whether things are Vulgar, Mythic Threads, the High and sometimes Middle Umbra, Dreaming, social constructs like economies): has loads of evidence, makes sense, adds up to a setting that makes sense.<br /> <br /> Consensus controls everything and it's all wibbly wobbly: <i>Marge Simpson holding a potato</i> &amp;quot;I just think it's neat!&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. The idea that all of the reality is just a mindscape, that it is all an illusion or that it's all just a creation of the senses, the idea of the &quot;immaterialism&quot; of Berkeley. The hindus had this conception for thousands of years, upon which the entire universe would be just Vishnu's (the Creator God) dream; this idea is also shared by Buddhism, upon which the world were we get reincarnated over and over is Maya - Ilusion - and that you must strive to reach the Nirvana - which we could say that is exactly to &quot;Awake&quot; from the illusions of the world and to remove oneself from the eternal cicle of reincarnation. Plato had the idea of the shadows in the cave, and Berkeley the theory of immaterialism. And the movie Matrix brought up a very interesting view on the nature of our reality.<br /> <br /> A world 100% built by the Consensus aint so deranged, it is in fact possible to have things be so, if so desired by the ST. I think this is left open and each table can desire the kind of world they want to deal with, from Matrix or Berkeley full immaterialism all the way up to the atheism of Niezstche and the materialism of the 19/20th century scientists and philosophers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T19:26:19-07:00","id":1491975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/798518-the-nature-of-the-consensus?p=1491938#post1491938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consensus controls everything and it's all wibbly wobbly: <i>Marge Simpson holding a potato</i> &amp;quot;I just think it's neat!&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, what would it take to convince 7 billions of people that Earth is a flat disc supported by 4 elephants on top of a &quot;cosmic turtle&quot; floating on the cosmic ocean, in order to provoke such a massive change on the reality of the universe enough for changing the law of gravity?<br /> <br /> Even if everything were 100% Consensus, I dont know that we would be able to notice any drastic difference in practical terms","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-07T14:55:05-07:00","id":1492558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/798518-the-nature-of-the-consensus#post798518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the nature of the Consensus?<br /> <br /> First, there's the \u201cConsensual Reality\u201d bit, in that Sleepers can't influence reality unless their collective beliefs are aligned: a minority view isn't going to be strong enough to overpower a majority view, all else being equal; and even a majority view may not take hold, if it's opposed by a substantial minority. There's also the matter of Mythic Threads and Hypernarratives, where minority beliefs <i>do</i> have some influence, generally by <i>not</i> directly opposing the majority view: see the last paragraph of the Significant Instruments box on p.588.<br /> <br /> Then there's the fact that Consensus beliefs tend to be localized \u2014 or, put another way, the Correspondence Range chart applies to the Consensus every bit as much as it does to the Awakened (likewise with other \u201cseparation factors\u201d such as the Time chart and Spirit's Gauntlet ratings; more on these below). The influence of any given Sleeper's beliefs is strongest in his immediate vicinity, and gets weaker as his familiarity with the subject decreases. This is where Reality Zones come from: the residents of a small town have more influence on the nature of reality in that town than they do in the neighboring town, and vice versa. This means that the VA efforts at getting Sleepers to transcend distance (culminating in the Internet) leads to a more homogeneous overall Consensus, as the influence of any given Sleeper can be spread far and wide. Ironically, the fact that the Consensus <i>isn't</i> homogeneous means that it's possible for localized reality zones to suffer from various types of Quiet: the entry for Irrationality Zones (under <i>Localized Reality</i>) ends with a mention of Irrationality Zones that have succumbed to Denial; and more generally, Irrationality Zones can be thought of as pockets of the Consensus that have succumbed to Quiet, usually manifesting as Madness.<br /> <br /> But third, you have Earthly Foundations: aspects of reality that prove stubbornly resistant to the influence of the Consensus. There are several schools of thought about why Earthly Foundations exist: there may indeed be certain truths that are hardwired into reality, and are innately true (what MRev referred to as Cosmological Constants; the opening paragraphs of Technocratic Reality implies that much of modern physics is in fact this kind of Earthly Foundation, with technomagick being an extrapolation on innate truths built into the fabric of reality); there may be influences from other times that are strong enough to endure even in the face of an opposing Consensus today (Historical Inertia; note that the nature of Time is such that the past influences the future much more readily than vice versa); and there may be inhuman entities capable of influencing reality, such as the Greater Spirit Entities mentioned on pp.486\u2013487 or rare Lesser Entities (same pages) that have somehow acquired Avatar-like abilities (arguably, the Technocray's efforts to strengthen the Gauntlet are as much to isolate Conventional Space from these ultraterrestrial influences, granting the Consensus of humanity more of a monopoly on this side of the barrier \u2014 which is only effective to the extent that the entity in question is confined to the other side). But regardless of <i>why</i>, the result is the same: there are some things that will be true (or false, as the case may be) even if the local consensus of humanity says otherwise. Note that this allows for a more widespread version of the aforementioned \u201cpockets of Quiet\u201d: an overall disbelief in an Earthly Foundation is arguably an overall case of Consensual Denial.<br /> <br /> That third point is especially significant, since it drives home an important truth \u2014 that the Consensus and Reality are <i>not</i> interchangeable terms: the Consensus <i>influences</i> Reality, just as the Awakened do; but it doesn't <i>define</i> Reality. Put more bluntly, Reality doesn't need Magick. This is something that mages generally don't dwell on, since accepting it requires a humility that tends to run counter to the pride that exists at the heart of Magick. But just because you don't believe something, that doesn't make it false.</div> </div> </div> </div>where is this text from? some book? you wrote it? I'm curious.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-07T21:47:01-07:00","id":1492569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/798518-the-nature-of-the-consensus?p=1492558#post1492558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> where is this text from? some book? you wrote it? I'm curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's from me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-08T03:23:47-07:00","id":1492583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/798518-the-nature-of-the-consensus?p=1492569#post1492569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's from me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it and mostly agree; I'm also curious because I've never seen the term &quot;Irrationality Zones&quot; or &quot;Quiet Zones&quot;, are these your creation too? If not, in which book can I read about them? (for context, I read M20 core completely, and all M20 books up to the Fallen; after Fallen I've not read anyone yet). Also, &quot;pp.487-488&quot; refers to which book?<br /> <br /> thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-08T03:42:55-07:00","id":1492584,"title":"","content":"Irrationality Zones are in M20, p.614. Greater Spirit Entities are mentioned in M20, pp.487\u2013488.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-08T05:54:47-07:00","id":1492590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/798518-the-nature-of-the-consensus?p=1492584#post1492584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Irrationality Zones are in M20, p.614. Greater Spirit Entities are mentioned in M20, pp.487\u2013488.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! I didn't remember those. \ud83e\udd17","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-10T08:58:31-07:00","id":1492762,"title":"","content":"<i>Throughout our world in this 21st century, the Technocratic vision of reality holds the coincidental edge, not simply because of the Union\u2019s indoctrination (although that does have something to do with it) but because science-based technology is rooted in following the laws of Earthly physics. Unlike faith and magic, it\u2019s based upon repeatable, verifiable, consistent results, not mere Enlightened Will, so it tends to work more reliably than mystic magick does.</i><br /> <br /> It's funny - I feel like this one quote from M20 very solidly lands on the side of &quot;science is real, it isn't just a result of a pro-science consensus&quot;, but I've never seen anyone talk about it before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-10T16:06:07-07:00","id":1492778,"title":"","content":"Yep. That's what I was referring to in this part of my first post: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/798518-the-nature-of-the-consensus#post798518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the opening paragraphs of Technocratic Reality implies that much of modern physics is in fact this kind of Earthly Foundation, with technomagick being an extrapolation on innate truths built into the fabric of reality</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a crucial part of my theory that the Technocracy <i>may have a valid point</i> when they insist that what they do is fundamentally (albeit very subtly) different from Willworking. <br /> <br /> That said, I see this as another \u201cBlind Men and the Elephant\u201d thing: to the Technocracy, it's all about Enlightenment: learning the secrets of the universe and using them to achieve the seemingly impossible; to the Traditions, it's all about Willworking. <br /> <br /> I go into a lot more detail about this sort of thing <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1338648#post1338648\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1375869#post1375869\">here</a>. I would recommend reading the entire thread; lots of cool philosophical speculation. Keep in mind while reading it, that it predates <b>Technocracy Reloaded</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-10-2022, 07:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-10T16:35:27-07:00","id":1492779,"title":"","content":"Oh; and here's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1433105-how-the-concept-of-logic-contradicts-consensual-reality\">another thread</a> that's worth reading. And <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra\">another one</a>. And <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1457982-materials-about-communism-socialism-in-mage-the-ascension-scenario\">another</a>. Also <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446626-anyone-else-dissapointed-with-article-4\">this</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-10-2022, 08:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T11:37:06-07:00","id":1492904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/798518-the-nature-of-the-consensus?p=1492762#post1492762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Throughout our world in this 21st century, the Technocratic vision of reality holds the coincidental edge, not simply because of the Union\u2019s indoctrination (although that does have something to do with it) but because science-based technology is rooted in following the laws of Earthly physics. Unlike faith and magic, it\u2019s based upon repeatable, verifiable, consistent results, not mere Enlightened Will, so it tends to work more reliably than mystic magick does.</i><br /> <br /> It's funny - I feel like this one quote from M20 very solidly lands on the side of &quot;science is real, it isn't just a result of a pro-science consensus&quot;, but I've never seen anyone talk about it before.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The flip side of this is that technology often stops working in the remote and unpopulated areas where there is no consensus around to prop it up. Even if the Technocracy is building on the more stable points of reality, their Sciences and sleeper science still require consensus. <br /> <br /> Also, I don't think the Technocracy is alone in seeking out the 'beams' of reality to build on. Mythic threads themselves are powerful foundations and bear much of the same character as Earthly Foundations. Instead the Technocracy is more methodical about it and prefers the ones with fewer barriers to use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-04T15:21:56-07:00","id":1494353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/798518-the-nature-of-the-consensus?p=1492904#post1492904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The flip side of this is that technology often stops working in the remote and unpopulated areas where there is no consensus around to prop it up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it, though? As written, Reality Zones only affect Awakened Magick/Enlightened Science: they shift the boundary of what's considered Vulgar vs. Coincidental, and they shift the difficulty of Arete/Enlightenment rolls. There's nothing anywhere about <i>mundane</i> technology failing in these remote Zones. <br /> <br /> I'm not <i>against</i> the idea that you're describing, per se; but it's not in the rules as written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-05T06:03:59-07:00","id":1494409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/798518-the-nature-of-the-consensus?p=1494353#post1494353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it, though? ... There's nothing anywhere about <i>mundane</i> technology failing in these remote Zones.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is, though:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M20 pg 615 Deep Wilderness</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Advanced technology tends to fail in deep-wilderness areas, but the oldest forms of magick thrive. The further a person gets from civilization, the less predictable Reality becomes.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't specify Technomagic or the efforts of the Technocracy, it says technology. The same distinction is made at several other nearby, including the Industrialized World writeup, so it is quite reasonable to accept it here. The Rural Areas writeup describes similar issues with modern technology (this time giving specific examples that are not Effects or Devices).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As written, Reality Zones only affect Awakened Magick/Enlightened Science: they shift the boundary of what's considered Vulgar vs. Coincidental, and they shift the difficulty of Arete/Enlightenment rolls. <br /> <br /> I'm not <i>against</i> the idea that you're describing, per se; but it's not in the rules as written. </div> </div> </div>As written, reality zones are a sliding scale that can be dialed from zero to completely change reality, with 'limited to Effects' being somewhere in the middle. The section that covers how reality zones affect Effects explicitly states that it is covering how the zones affect <i>mages</i> in game terms, which makes sense as that is the aspect of reality zones that is going to come up most frequently and have the most mechanical effect.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-06T10:33:21-07:00","id":1494458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/798518-the-nature-of-the-consensus?p=1494409#post1494409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is, though:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It doesn't specify Technomagic or the efforts of the Technocracy, it says technology. The same distinction is made at several other nearby, including the Industrialized World writeup, so it is quite reasonable to accept it here. The Rural Areas writeup describes similar issues with modern technology (this time giving specific examples that are not Effects or Devices).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As written, reality zones are a sliding scale that can be dialed from zero to completely change reality, with 'limited to Effects' being somewhere in the middle. The section that covers how reality zones affect Effects explicitly states that it is covering how the zones affect <i>mages</i> in game terms, which makes sense as that is the aspect of reality zones that is going to come up most frequently and have the most mechanical effect.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. In a very loose way to describe it, it would be the in-game answer to why your cellphone doesnt have any signal if you're in the middle of a jungle (as opposed to lacking a reception tower in real life). One could assume however that in a Reality Zone even further away from techno paradigm would make your celular completely break.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}